    {
      "id": "15",
      "type": "writeup",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 15,
        "body_ja": "",
        "body": "<p><span data-gp-id='71'>ね</span> is classified as a <span data-term='終助詞・しゅうじょし'>sentence ending particle</span> in Japanese. It may also be pronounced as <span data-gp-id='71'>ねえ</span>. <span data-gp-id='71'>ね</span> is used when the speaker is looking for agreement from someone, or wants confirmation about something. Due to this, it is often translated as 'right?', or 'isn't it?'. To use <span data-gp-id='71'>ね</span>, simply add it to the end of almost any sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154735'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154736'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154737'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154738'></ul>\r\n\r\n<p>As we will cover in our lesson about the sentence ending particle <span data-gp-id='66'>な</span>, <span data-gp-id='71'>ね</span> can almost be thought of as the opposite. <span data-gp-id='71'>ね</span> is used when expressing a shared opinion, a shared thought, or generally something you think will be agreed with by the listener. However, な focuses almost exclusively on the speaker, and their own thoughts.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154739'>\r\n<li data-study-question='154740'></ul>\r\n\r\n<section class='funfact'><h4>Fun Fact</h4>\r\n<p><span data-gp-id='78'>よ</span> and <span data-gp-id='71'>ね</span> are very frequently combined together to make the sentence ender <span data-gp-id='78'>よ</span><span data-gp-id='71'>ね</span>. This is used purely when you expect the listener will agree with you.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='183756'></ul></section>\r\n\r\n<section class='caution'><h4>Caution</h4>\r\n<p><span data-gp-id='71'>ね</span> is much weaker than <span data-gp-id='9'>でしょう</span> or <span data-gp-id='18'>だろう</span>, and is sometimes said purely out of habit, without much nuance of 'right' at all.</p></section>"
      }
    },
